  618 f338:             ;
  619 f338:             ; O command: boot. Read the boot block (LBA 0) to OSBASE, check 'P8' and OSCNT, read OSCNT sectors from LBA 1
  620 f338:             ; to OSBASE and call it; the OS returns with RET.
  621 f338:             ;
  622 f338:             ;
  623 f338:             ; ':' - Intel-hex loader (YACC1-D 2026-09-23). A ':' at the prompt starts load mode: the rest of the record is read
  624 f338:             ; without echo (uartinne), its bytes stored from its address on, and the record acknowledged with one character:
  625 f338:             ;   .  stored and the checksum is right
  626 f338:             ;   ?  a bad hex digit or a bad checksum
  627 f338:             ;   !  refused or not verified: an address outside $1000-$DFFF (the monitor's page, the stack and the ROM are
  628 f338:             ;      protected; any write to $E000-$FFFF would reach the 28C64, review M2), or the byte read back differently
  629 f338:             ; Between records everything up to the next ':' is skipped (CR, LF, blanks), so an assembler .img can be pasted into
  630 f338:             ; a terminal or sent as is; ESC (or a NUL, the emulators' end of input) abandons, between records or inside one. The end record (type 01) prints
  631 f338:             ; LOADED, or LOADED WITH ERRORS when any record failed, and returns to the prompt. Records of other types are read
  632 f338:             ; and checked but not stored. Host side: tools/monload.py paces the characters (the UART has no FIFO enabled: one
  633 f338:             ; character of buffering) and waits for each acknowledgement. Registers: R3 checksum, R4 count, R5 type,
  634 f338:             ; R6 record status (0 ok, 1 bad hex, 2 refused/unverified), R7 the address; never R2.
  635 f338:             ;
  636 f338:             hexload:
  637 f338: 0d 05               LDTI  LOADMODE
  638 f33a: e7 0f 00            STT   monmode
  639 f33d: 0d 00               LDTI  0
  640 f33f: e7 0f 01            STT   lderr
  641 f342:             ldrec:
  642 f342: 1b 00 00            MVIW  R3,0
  643 f345: 1c 00 00            MVIW  R4,0
  644 f348: 1e 00 00            MVIW  R6,0
  645 f34b: 04 f3 f3            JSR   ldbyte            ; byte count
  646 f34e: 34                  MVARL R4
  647 f34f: 04 f3 f3            JSR   ldbyte            ; address high
  648 f352: 3f                  MVARH R7
  649 f353: 04 f3 f3            JSR   ldbyte            ; address low
  650 f356: 37                  MVARL R7
  651 f357: 04 f3 f3            JSR   ldbyte            ; record type
  652 f35a: 35                  MVARL R5
